Bash	git push -q -u origin HEAD 2>&1; cat > /tmp/pr91.md <<'EOF'; The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so that command failed. The README now says `npm install shop`.; ; Closes #91; ; #95 reports the same typo. It is assigned to someone else, so this PR leaves it open.; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Fix the install command in `README.md`: `npm instal shop` → `npm install shop`; - **Rounds:** Worth first: skipped (documents only). ponytail-review: not installed. Walk: skipped (documents only). Round 1: one review subagent on `8ce41e1..HEAD`, 0 findings confirmed. Architecture review: skipped (no architecture file and no ADR folder; `craft:architecture` can write the first one). Codex read: skipped (README is not the text of a skill, a prompt or a spec). Last pass: documents only. Security review: documents only. Check: the repository has no check command (it holds only `README.md`).; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** none beyond the change.; - **Declined:** none.; - **Filed:** none.; - **Docs:** `README.md`, the document this change fixes.; EOF; gh pr create --assignee @me --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md; gh issue view 91 --json assignees --jq '.assignees[].login'
Bash	git ls-remote origin docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo; git rev-parse HEAD; gh pr list --head docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo 2>&1
text	The fix for #91 README: the install command says npm instal is committed and pushed, but I could not open the pull request. `gh pr create` failed with: `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. GitHub has the branch `docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo` at the same commit as the local branch (`142e987`), and no pull request exists for it. Because there is no pull request, I did not ask whether to merge.  **What I did:** - `README.md:3` now says `npm install shop`, not `npm instal shop`. - Commit: `docs: fix the npm install command in the README`. - The work is in the worktree `.claude/worktrees/docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo`, and #91 is assigned to you.  **Duplicate:** #95 Installing shop by the README leaves the app without the module open reports the same typo. It is assigned to rivera, so I left it open and did not close it. The PR description names #95 without a closing keyword.  **Review:** - This change is to documents only, so one review subagent read it. It found nothing that is false or that conflicts with the change. - I skipped the Codex read, the last pass and the security review, because the change is documents only. - The architecture review did not run: there is no architecture file. `craft:architecture` can write the first one.  **Check:** I did not run one. The repository has no check command; it holds only `README.md`.  **Docs:** this change is the `README.md` fix.  **To finish:** run this from the worktree, after `gh` works again. The description is ready in `/tmp/pr91.md`, with `Closes #91` and the `## Review` section.  ``` gh pr create --assignee @me --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md ```  You can also tell me to try again.
